        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    higher_strike_price = 155\n    lower_strike_price = 145\n    cost_of_higher_strike = 5\n    revenue_from_lower_strike = 2\n    underlying_at_expiration = 140\n    shares_per_contract = 100\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    net_cost_of_spread = (\n        cost_of_higher_strike - revenue_from_lower_strike\n    ) * shares_per_contract\n\n    spread_value_at_expiration = (\n        higher_strike_price - lower_strike_price\n    ) * shares_per_contract\n\n    profit_or_loss = spread_value_at_expiration - net_cost_of_spread\n\n    # return answer\n    return round(profit_or_loss)\n```",
